1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,200
In Henan's Taihang Mountains, a tunnel cuts a cliff.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,400
You'd assume a state crew blasted it.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,600
Thirteen villagers carved it by hand.

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,000
Their village, Guoliang, had one way out.

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,400
A crumbling staircase up a sheer rock face.

7
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,800
So in 1972, they picked up hammers.

8
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,600
Five years. 4,000 hammers. 12 tons of steel.

9
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,000
Double-tap for the thirteen who dug it.

10
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,400
One man died. It opened in 1977.

11
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,400
Expert Tip: ride the village bus through — the carved windows frame the valley.

12
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,200
Could your town have built this? Tell me below.
